cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Australian Raptor CNN + AUSLAN: Deep-learning identification of Australian birds of prey with inclusive sign-language vocabulary"
type: software
version: "1.5.0"
date-released: "2026-06-07"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ZOMBIECRAFTIAN/raptor-australia"
abstract: >-
  A YOLO-assisted EfficientNetB4 computer-vision pipeline for
  identifying eight Australian raptor species, paired with a
  provisional Australian Sign Language (AUSLAN) vocabulary for
  accessible citizen science. The dataset is sourced from
  iNaturalist Australia and the Atlas of Living Australia.
  Observations can be exported in Darwin Core format for upload to
  the Atlas of Living Australia and other GBIF data publishers.
keywords:
  - "computer vision"
  - "convolutional neural networks"
  - "biodiversity"
  - "raptors"
  - "Australia"
  - "AUSLAN"
  - "deep learning"
  - "transfer learning"
  - "Darwin Core"
authors:
  - family-names: "Fernandez Baez"
    given-names: "Brian"
    affiliation: "Instituto Tecnologico Nacional de Mexico, Campus Veracruz"
    orcid: ""
    # Computer Systems Engineer with a specialisation in Advanced
    # Computational Concurrency. Independent researcher applying
    # deep-learning identification methods to Australian raptor
    # biodiversity and inclusive science (AUSLAN).
